From: OpenWrt
Subject: tools: do not statically link host tools on macOS

The host tools default to "-static", which the only Apple special case
(darwin-ppc) overrides but modern macOS does not match: uname -m maps to
HOSTARCH=arm on Apple Silicon, so the build falls through to the generic
"-static" and fails ("library 'crt0.o' not found") because Apple's linker
does not support fully static binaries. Clear HOST_LDFLAGS on any darwin
host. Static linking of these build-time helpers is not required.

This should be fixed upstream as well.

--- a/tools/Makefile
+++ b/tools/Makefile
@@ -113,6 +113,11 @@
 HOST_LDFLAGS =
 endif
 
+# Apple's linker does not support fully static binaries (no crt0.o).
+ifeq ($(HOSTOS),darwin)
+HOST_LDFLAGS =
+endif
+
 #
 # Include this after HOSTOS HOSTARCH check
 # so that we can act intelligently.
